==A quick update on the 'RoboSpear' hotfix - Thursday, October 30th==
Hello! If you've been looking at OSRS content or talking about it with your friends in the past 12 hours, you'll undoubtedly have stumbled across the 'RoboSpear', a strategy for Yama developed by jeremiah855 and Muffyn. If you have absolutely no idea what we're talking about, then check out [https://youtu.be/a2NqCpXz-QU this absolutely wonderful video] that highlights just how far OSRS has come from 'medieval clicking simulator' and watch how talented players embarked on a full-blown data science project to optimise combat against the Master of Pacts.

<center>
{{Youtube|a2NqCpXz-QU}}
</center>

In essence, this method makes use of the Blue Moon Spear's special attack - which increases accuracy and damage for every tick of 'binding' removed from an enemy - to deal a huge hit of up to 200 damage to Yama in his third phase, with the added benefit of him moving around the arena once this bind is 'consumed' by the spear, enabling a brand new kiting method.

Late last night we deployed a hotfix to cap this damage, which has understandably ruffled a few feathers, so we're here to explain ourselves!

We'd like to make clear that Yama is not the only NPC in game that has a 'bind' applied this way, last night's hotfix was a quick fix to give us assurances that the team wouldn't wake up tomorrow and find bosses all over the game being absolutely obliterated by the Blue Moon Spear and armour set.

This morning, we spent some time discussing the 'RoboSpear' as a team and want to share our thoughts:

* As we said above, other NPCs are 'bound' in the same way. While we think this interaction is very cool and love what it does for Yama, we don't want to risk other NPCs being effectively one-shottable by a mid-game armour set. Similarly, we'll take a safety pass at other NPCs that are bound in this way to make sure there aren't scenarios where thing like Verzik P2 suddenly starts walking around.
* The existing cap of 200 is a global damage cap as a guardrail for the whole game. There's a chance that future bosses might have unique mechanics that allow players to deal astronomical damage where we might like to increase this cap, which would buff these Blue Moon interactions further.
* In general, hitting 200s with mid-game gear that isn't tailored towards a specific weakness (e.g. the Keris Partisan) just doesn't feel right. Particularly when this large damage nuke is very accessible, and shaves time off of the toughest and most engaging phase of the fight in particular.

Having said all of that, we think the RoboSpear and the work that's gone into developing the method is really cool, so rather than removing emergent gameplay - we'd like to balance it, similar to the Araxxor step-under from release.

That means we'd like to raise the 'cap' on how many ticks of binding we use to calculate the Blue Moon Spear's bonus Special Attack damage up to 75, which should leave its max hit at around 100. We'll also be keeping the 'unbind' functionality of the attack, so the lossless cycle enabled by releasing Yama from his own programming will still be doable, meaning it should still be 'meta' for anybody looking for the fastest runs on average. Finally, we'll be separating the accuracy boost from the damage boost on the Blue Moon Spear special attack, this was something of an oversight in our initial fix but due to Yama's high Crush defence, the capping of the Spear's Special Attack also resulted in 0s being almost guaranteed - which was never our intent.

Note that we'll keep this damage cap in place at other NPCs in case new and weird stuff starts to pop up, but we're always eager to encourage experimentation with gear setups and strategies: emergent gameplay is a huge part of what makes OSRS special and we never want to clip the wings of players looking to make new discoveries or discourage people from sharing cool finds!

We appreciate your understanding and hope that you can accept why the 'better safe than sorry' approach that we took with last night's hotfix was a tad sudden, and our willingness to maintain this cool interaction but tweak to make it more appropriate. We'll also be taking a look at making necessary changes behind the scenes to make sure similar interactions can't break other NPCs around the game in damaging ways, but we're more than fine with Yama getting some extra steps in during P3!

Now it's time for you to get out there, mark a bunch of crazy tiles spit out by computing wizardry, panic-buy Blue Moon gear and shave some ticks off of your Yama PB - he doesn't mind, he's just happy to <s>claim your soul for all eternity</s> see you!

